  "title": "Tamara M NDE 5415",
  "date": "Dicembre1992",
  "content": "I was undergoing surgery during a termination of pregnancy. Suddenly, I was aware of myself and I was getting up from the surgery table. As I was rising, I found myself hovering upward and I turned only to see myself lying on the surgery table. There was copious bleeding on the floor and a rush of nurses and physicians around my body on the table. I could see everything from above. I felt nothing, no emotions or thoughts. I was moving in the air endowed with the conscience of BEING. Later, I awoke in a bed and I was receiving a blood transfusion. The doctor said that during my intervention a hemorrhage, which they could not stop, took them by surprise. That was why I was under intravenous treatment now. They were transferring several liters of blood into my body. I told the doctor that I knew it because I had seen it all. He stood puzzled, for he said, while in surgery, I was under total anesthesia.",
